<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">The conventional test the speculation must still pass</p>
    <h2 id="t-sakharov">Separation Is Not Baryogenesis</h2>
    <p>For a universe beginning with zero net baryon number to end with a genuine global excess, conventional
      baryogenesis requires the Sakharov conditions: baryon-number violation, C and CP violation, and a
      departure from thermal equilibrium. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span> These allow reactions to create a
      bias and cosmic expansion to prevent the inverse reactions from erasing it.</p>
    <p>The phase-sector proposal takes a different route only if the global excess remains zero:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      B_{\mathrm{visible}}=-B_{\mathrm{complement}},
      \qquad B_{\mathrm{total}}=0.
    \]</p>
    <p>It can then replace global baryogenesis with local sorting. But that does not make the problem vanish.
      The earlier interaction must still correlate matter with one sector and antimatter with the other. If
      the sorting is exactly symmetric, our matter branch is one member of a complementary pair. If one sign
      is dynamically preferred, CP violation has returned through the side door.</p>
    <p>Nor should the complementary sector casually be called ordinary antimatter. If it cannot share our
      strong and electromagnetic vertices, it is a hidden CPT-related sector. Its contents may be conjugate
      to ours while its phenomenology resembles mirror or dark matter. The name must follow the coupling,
      not the poetry.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">What the idea volunteers for examination</p>
    <h2 id="t-tests">Five Debts That Can Become Tests</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>One &mdash; define the sector</h3>
      <p>Name the observable or quantum number that makes the two states orthogonal. A plane in a picture is
        not yet a degree of freedom in a theory.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Two &mdash; write the portal</h3>
      <p>Specify the operator that permits gravity, mixing or occasional conversion while suppressing strong
        and electromagnetic annihilation. Its coupling must be calculable.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Three &mdash; survive the hot universe</h3>
      <p>Integrate the annihilation rate through the high-density era and show that the proposed residue is
        not erased before nucleosynthesis or excessively injected into radiation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Four &mdash; count the hidden energy</h3>
      <p>A gravitating complementary sector affects expansion, structure, lensing and the radiation budget.
        Those effects must fit the cosmic microwave background and light-element abundances.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Five &mdash; identify the clock</h3>
      <p>Periodic and quasiperiodic models require a physical tick, a linewidth and a map from phase to
        interaction strength. Without them, recurrence counts geometry rather than events.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>The clean failure</h3>
      <p>If the sectors have ordinary overlap, if the hidden abundance violates cosmological limits, or if
        no interaction can sort baryon sign by sector, the proposal fails rather than retreating into an
        unobservable plane.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">A synthesis, not a fourth escape</p>
    <h2 id="t-hybrid">A Weak Phase-Dependent Portal</h2>
    <p>The most durable version combines approximate orthogonality with a small, phase-dependent opening:</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \Gamma_{\mathrm{ann}}
      =\Gamma_0\,\epsilon^2F(\Delta\theta),
      \qquad \epsilon\ll1.
    \]</p>
    <p>The factor \(\epsilon^2\) provides survival. The function \(F\) supplies either periodic windows or
      quasiperiodic leakage. This avoids demanding that a decimal inequality perform the work of a symmetry,
      while preserving an observational edge: a hidden complement is almost inaccessible, not inaccessible
      by definition.</p>
    <p>It is also the version most faithful to the residue picture. The previous interaction need not be
      recoverable in detail. Its unmatched products can persist because the channel that once joined them has
      nearly closed. What remains is not evidence of victory. It is evidence of incomplete contact.
      <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <h2 id="t-ledger">Earned, Chosen, Refused</h2>
    <dl class="glossary">
      <dt>Earned</dt>
      <dd>Pair annihilation preserves the signed baryon difference. A global phase alone does not change an
        overlap probability. Orthogonal modes can forbid a matrix element. The cyclic five-to-eight and
        five-to-four clocks close after forty and twenty ticks respectively. Irrational logarithmic phases
        never exactly repeat but return arbitrarily close. Reversible fine-grained dynamics can display a
        two-sided rise of coarse-grained entropy.</dd>
      <dt>Chosen</dt>
      <dd>That visible matter is the residue of an earlier interaction; that complementary antimatter was
        sorted into another sector; that both sectors may source one gravitational field; and that their
        interaction is permanently, periodically or quasiperiodically suppressed.</dd>
      <dt>Refused</dt>
      <dd>Calling an ordinary phase factor a barrier. Claiming that annihilation creates a signed excess.
        Treating exact arithmetic non-alignment as zero physical coupling. Calling hidden matter antimatter
        without specifying the conjugation. Using an unseen plane to evade every possible test.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="kicker">Closing stance</p>
    <p class="lede">Matter may be not what defeated antimatter, but what remained unmatched when an earlier
      interaction divided, paired and cancelled the two.</p>
    <p>If the complement survives, its absence from our instruments must be caused by a structure precise
      enough to calculate: a conserved orthogonality, a narrow recurring window, or a quasiperiodic portal
      with a finite rate. Until that structure exists, the thought is a disciplined possibility rather than
      a physical theory.</p>
    <p class="muted small">Read the geometrical origin of the proposal in
      <a href="/moebius/#t-cp">Matter, Antimatter, and the Möbius Berry Phase</a>, and compare its clocks on
      <a href="/prime-plane/">The Prime Plane</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
